1. WHAT IS FILEBEAT?
====================================================================

Filebeat is a lightweight log shipper.

Purpose

Collect logs

↓

Send logs

↓

Logstash / Elasticsearch

Very Low CPU Usage

Very Low Memory Usage

Developed by Elastic.

====================================================================
2. FILEBEAT ARCHITECTURE
====================================================================

Log File

↓

Harvester

↓

Input

↓

Processors

↓

Output

↓

Logstash

or

Elasticsearch

====================================================================
3. HARVESTER
====================================================================

Harvester is responsible for reading a single log file.

Example

/var/log/messages

↓

One Harvester

Another Log File

↓

Another Harvester

Every file has its own Harvester.

====================================================================
4. INPUT
====================================================================

Input tells Filebeat

Which logs to monitor.

Example

filestream

log (Old)

stdin

Most Common

filestream

====================================================================
5. FILESTREAM
====================================================================

Modern Filebeat Input.

Replaces old "log" input.

Better Performance.

Better File Rotation Handling.

Lower Resource Usage.

====================================================================
6. PROCESSORS
====================================================================

Processors modify events before sending.

Examples

add_host_metadata

add_cloud_metadata

add_docker_metadata

drop_fields

drop_event

rename

decode_json_fields

====================================================================
7. OUTPUT
====================================================================

Filebeat supports multiple outputs.

Common Outputs

Logstash

Elasticsearch

Kafka

Redis

Console

File

Most Common

Logstash

Elasticsearch

====================================================================
8. REGISTRY FILE
====================================================================

Very Important.

Registry stores

Current Read Position

(File Offset)

Purpose

Avoid duplicate log reading.

If Filebeat restarts,

Reading starts from previous offset.

Not from beginning.

====================================================================
9. OFFSET
====================================================================

Offset means

Current byte position inside log file.

Example

100 MB Log

Offset

25 MB

Means

25 MB already read.

====================================================================
10. MULTILINE
====================================================================

Used for

Java Exceptions

Python Traceback

Stack Traces

Instead of

10 Events

↓

One Event

